  "why": "the first probe read --as-numbered-lines, whose line list cannot separate carried lines from context away from -U0; PROTOCOL.md Amendment 3"
 },
 "verdict": "At -U0: 2 of 4 rows over-stage at exit 0, and the tool's own output names the carried line in every one. Away from -U0: 12 of 12 rows over-stage at exit 0, and the tool's own primary output names a line beyond the want in 12 of 12 -- C11 holds the walk to git's own statement of the index on all 16 rows where anything was staged, and C12 shows the walk reports an exact selection as exactly that line. K3 therefore fails at every context measured, not only at -U0: the negative is a property of the tool's output, not of the pipeline's context. `-U0` remains load-bearing for correctness -- away from it filterdiff over-stages every case probed -- but not for auditability.",
 "verdict_state": "observed"
}
